                        "form": "méprisantes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "53e72097-2a5d-3697-b0ba-53b104edec4a",
                        "entry_id": "739c82b0-f8c8-3848-9b4d-ee55ba6003d1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui marque du mépris."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b697ceb8-f959-4122-a92f-9a8ff1868c80",
                                "sense_id": "53e72097-2a5d-3697-b0ba-53b104edec4a",
                                "text": "Quoique très instruite, elle n'avoit ni les caprices, ni l’humeur qu'on attribue aux gens de lettres, qui tantôt se livrent à une loquacité importune, tantôt se renferment dans un silence méprisant."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "94e6676f-140b-4e0e-b85f-4865d1643d02",
                                "sense_id": "53e72097-2a5d-3697-b0ba-53b104edec4a",
                                "text": "Vous avez, docteur, de bien curieuses fréquentations, dit-il d'un ton un peu méprisant, un représentant de ces mauvais moines adorateurs du démon ! Que les Chinois sérieux estiment un peu plus qu'un soldat, mais un peu moins qu'une prostituée !"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f8bbc2fd-2c0b-4193-ad44-4a25c05f1f83",
                                "sense_id": "53e72097-2a5d-3697-b0ba-53b104edec4a",
                                "text": "Il suffit de faire un tour sous des posts récents des chercheuses pour lire un certain nombre de réponses méprisantes ou dénialistes."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "000b7a9c-f562-4063-9bfd-fef2bcd71d37",
                        "source_entry_id": "739c82b0-f8c8-3848-9b4d-ee55ba6003d1",
                        "source_sense_id": "53e72097-2a5d-3697-b0ba-53b104edec4a",
                        "target_lang_word": "contemptuous",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "contemptuous",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a7b06e1e-4e94-3e60-963a-efe04bd3481b",
                                        "entry_id": "3ef8152b-1171-3fe3-8841-a262cad9c984",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Showing contempt; expressing disdain; showing a lack of respect."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d76e8b5e-c1dc-4569-ad89-0ccab3eb900e",
                                                "sense_id": "a7b06e1e-4e94-3e60-963a-efe04bd3481b",
                                                "text": "I don't know that guy, but he just gave me a contemptuous look."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e4762f8a-2b73-4715-83f0-b66f6424cbbe",
                                                "sense_id": "a7b06e1e-4e94-3e60-963a-efe04bd3481b",
                                                "text": "Sir George burst into a loud fit of contemptuous laughter."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "76ca044e-1bc9-4325-a20d-5be0176c378f",
                                                "sense_id": "a7b06e1e-4e94-3e60-963a-efe04bd3481b",
                                                "text": "The most rapid and most seductive transition in all human nature is that which attends the palliation of a ravenous appetite.[…]Can those harmless but refined fellow-diners be the selfish cads whose gluttony and personal appearance so raised your contemptuous wrath on your arrival?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "029f7d00-a73a-3707-9e72-d58398a4c2e4",
                                        "entry_id": "3ef8152b-1171-3fe3-8841-a262cad9c984",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Worthy of contempt; contemptible."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "rare"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f37d6c57-e3b3-4708-977a-f220a1bc6e34",
                                                "sense_id": "029f7d00-a73a-3707-9e72-d58398a4c2e4",
                                                "text": "Rep. Noble told GCN that she, however, had deep concern \"regarding the scandalous sexual exploitation and abuse of young children by adults.\" Noble has called on the community to \"support the efforts of the Suffolk County District Attorney's office in unraveling this contemptuous situation."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ecb82728-4a41-427e-8d5b-b4145169bc01",
                        "source_entry_id": "739c82b0-f8c8-3848-9b4d-ee55ba6003d1",
                        "source_sense_id": "53e72097-2a5d-3697-b0ba-53b104edec4a",
                        "target_lang_word": "scornful",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "scornful",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bfc9b8b5-1f53-3c5f-9b3d-66c1e42fc019",
                                        "entry_id": "05c305cc-7cb4-337c-8d1d-7220b12f588e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Showing scorn or disrespect; contemptuous; scathing; withering."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a0b466e8-5406-4f0f-b0a2-2c4f313c575a",
                                                "sense_id": "bfc9b8b5-1f53-3c5f-9b3d-66c1e42fc019",
                                                "text": "Bleſſed is that man that hath not walked in the counſaile of the vngodly: nor ſtand in the waye of ſynners, and hath not ſit in the ſeate of ſkornefull."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e81dd10d-324c-46f2-8bcb-02858ca276e6",
                                                "sense_id": "bfc9b8b5-1f53-3c5f-9b3d-66c1e42fc019",
                                                "text": "Fie, fie, vnknit that thretaning vnkinde brovv, / And dart not ſcornefull glances from thoſe eies, / To vvound thy Lord, thy King, thy Gouernour."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c1ebefb3-d96d-40d3-b021-7aa1b3a3cb80",
                                                "sense_id": "bfc9b8b5-1f53-3c5f-9b3d-66c1e42fc019",
                                                "text": "Elbows almost touching they leaned at ease, idly reading the almost obliterated lines engraved there. \"I never understood it,\" she observed, lightly scornful. \"What occult meaning has a sun-dial for the spooney? I'm sure I don't want to read riddles in a strange gentleman's optics.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1f32ccfc-1c11-45fc-adf5-d8c2f481a220",
                        "source_entry_id": "739c82b0-f8c8-3848-9b4d-ee55ba6003d1",
                        "source_sense_id": "53e72097-2a5d-3697-b0ba-53b104edec4a",
                        "target_lang_word": "minachtend",
                        "target_lang_code": "nl",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
